From 4f126619465de14954fdb345deb58c260ebeba9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Egorov <sergey.egorov@pruvendo.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 16:40:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] exchange: USDCBridge 12-PI chain-binding deposits +
 source allowlist
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upgrades finalizeDeposit to the deposit circuit's chain-binding v2 layout and
adds the two source-authenticity guards Alina's circuit review asked for:

- Public inputs 11 → 12: `chainId` inserted at instance #4 (proof-bound, MPT
  under transactionsRoot). `_parsePublicInputs` now reads 9 Fr and shifts
  dappId → fr[5]|fr[6], anAccount → fr[7]|fr[8]; DepositPI gains `chainId`.
- Source allowlist: `_expectedBridgeFr[chainId]` must equal the proof-bound
  `contractAddr` (rejects unknown chains, incl. empty-RLP chainId 0, and pins
  the trusted bridge per chain). Owner-populated via `setExpectedBridge`,
  fail-closed.
- Cross-dApp replay guard: proof-bound `dappId` must equal `_expectedAnDappId`
  (owner-set via `setExpectedAnDappId`).
- VK_BLOB rotated to the regenerated 12-PI Hermez VkBlob
  (sha256 3e2a2db2…bf0d049c, 5006 B, shape [17,13]) produced after the
  deposit-circuit soundness fixes; validated end-to-end through the tvm-sdk
  ZKHALO2VERIFYWITHVK opcode (deposit_10proofs: 4/4 tests pass).

The allowlist is intentionally NOT threaded through the onCodeUpgrade
migration cell (avoids coupling to zerostate deploy tooling); it must be
re-seeded by the owner after any code upgrade. DepositVoucher key
(depositId, contractAddr, dappId) is unchanged — no voucher re-embed needed.

New errors: ERR_UNKNOWN_SOURCE (222), ERR_WRONG_DAPP (223).

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
