From 21a781e7ae1972f2a5a9c24b92433493ceca999c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Egorov <sergey.egorov@pruvendo.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 15:35:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] exchange: put srcChainId in the deposit identity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The anti-replay identity was (depositId, contractAddr, dappId), which does not
separate source chains. `dappId` is one constant per deployment, `depositId` is a
per-chain counter that every chain starts at 0, and one bridge address routinely
serves several chains (CREATE2, or the same deployer nonce). So as soon as a
second chain is allowlisted and shares an address with the first, their deposits
collide: the second voucher deploy lands on the existing account, its constructor
is a no-op, `confirmDeposit` never fires, nothing mints. With the ETH-side refund
path retired in Phase 4.3 the user's funds have no way out. Not an attack — just
arithmetic, and it fires on the first multi-chain deposit rather than under
adversarial conditions.

`chainId` is already a proof-bound public input (#4) and already in scope where
the hash is built, so it costs nothing to include. Also threaded through the
voucher callback and `DepositFinalized`, so per-chain accounting and monitoring
can tell the chains apart.

The identity hash now lives in `_depositIdentity` rather than being spelled out
three times. Note that the third copy is in DepositVoucher's constructor and
cannot be shared: bridge and voucher must agree byte-for-byte, and a divergence
does not fail loudly — the voucher aborts on cell underflow (exit_code 9) before
reaching `confirmDeposit`, so deposits just stop minting, as happened on
2026-07-02. `acki-nacki-bridge/scripts/check_voucher_abi_consistency.py` now
checks all three copies plus the compiled artefacts.

**Both artefacts must be recompiled and redeployed together**, and the bridge
must re-embed the fresh `_depositVoucherCode` — the voucher ABI changed.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
 contracts/exchange/DepositVoucher.sol | 44 ++++++++++++++++++-------
 contracts/exchange/USDCBridge.sol     | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 71 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/contracts/exchange/DepositVoucher.sol b/contracts/exchange/DepositVoucher.sol
index 42451f4fc..9e87ac24d 100644
--- a/contracts/exchange/DepositVoucher.sol
+++ b/contracts/exchange/DepositVoucher.sol
@@ -11,22 +11,44 @@ import "./USDCBridge.sol";
 ///         account and the second constructor call is a no-op — natural
 ///         replay protection.
 contract DepositVoucher is USDCBridgeModifiers {
-    string constant version = "1.0.0";
+    // 2.0.0 — constructor takes `srcChainId` (breaking; must be redeployed
+    // together with the USDCBridge that embeds this code).
+    string constant version = "2.0.0";
 
-    /// @notice Hash of the proof-bound deposit identity (deposit_id,
-    ///         contract_addr, dapp_id). Forms the deterministic address of this
-    ///         voucher. amount/recipient are deliberately NOT hashed: they are
-    ///         fixed by the proof, so keying the replay slot on the identity
-    ///         alone makes one L1 deposit = one voucher = one mint, and a replay
-    ///         can never re-route the payout (same identity ⇒ same voucher).
+    /// @notice Hash of the proof-bound deposit identity (src_chain_id,
+    ///         deposit_id, contract_addr, dapp_id). Forms the deterministic
+    ///         address of this voucher. amount/recipient are deliberately NOT
+    ///         hashed: they are fixed by the proof, so keying the replay slot on
+    ///         the identity alone makes one L1 deposit = one voucher = one mint,
+    ///         and a replay can never re-route the payout (same identity ⇒ same
+    ///         voucher).
+    ///
+    ///         `src_chain_id` is in the identity because the other three do not
+    ///         separate chains: `dapp_id` is one constant per deployment,
+    ///         `deposit_id` is a per-chain counter starting at 0, and one bridge
+    ///         address commonly serves several chains. Without it, two
+    ///         allowlisted chains collide and the second deposit is silently
+    ///         swallowed as a replay.
     uint256 static _depositHash;
 
     /// @notice Deploy callback: forwards confirmation to USDCBridge so it mints
     ///         USDC for the proof-bound AN recipient. Only callable by USDCBridge.
-    /// @dev    The identity params (depositId, contractAddr, dappId) are bound to
-    ///         `_depositHash`; amount + recipient (anAccount) ride
+    /// @dev    The identity params (srcChainId, depositId, contractAddr, dappId)
+    ///         are bound to `_depositHash`; amount + recipient (anAccount) ride
     ///         through to `confirmDeposit` for the payout.
