From 1fb5b28c5fee915678cddfdbabe5c5f83910617a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Egorov <sergey.egorov@pruvendo.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 15:38:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] exchange: M-of-N attesters for the canonical-chain anchor
 set
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The anchor set that gates finalizeDeposit had one writer: the owner key. That was
the interim, and the whole point of storing a hash rather than a header was that
swapping the writer would not touch finalizeDeposit. This is that swap.

`attestBlockHash(chainId, blockHash)` is called as an external message signed by
an attester key, so the vote is attributed to `msg.pubkey()` — a key outside the
set cannot vote, and a key inside it cannot vote twice. Once `_attesterThreshold`
distinct attesters agree on a pair, the anchor is admitted. Votes for an
already-admitted pair are a no-op rather than an error: a peer arriving late has
done nothing wrong, and rejecting it would turn a benign race into an alert.

`disableOwnerAnchors()` is the call that actually reduces the trust assumption.
Until it is made the attester set is decoration, because the owner can still
admit any hash alone; after it, `attestBlockHash` is the only writer. One-way,
with no re-enable — a switch back would leave the owner key on the path
regardless of where it sits in the sequence — and it requires a satisfiable
attester set first so it cannot brick the only working writer.

Thresholds are kept satisfiable at both ends: `setAttesterThreshold` rejects 0
(which would admit on a single vote) and anything above the key count, and
removing a key re-checks the same bound, since otherwise a removal silently
freezes every future anchor.

What this does not fix: the threshold only helps if the attesters fail
independently. N keys held by one operator, or N attesters all reading the same
RPC provider, is one key wearing N hats. Each attester still owes the two
obligations no contract can enforce — resolve the hash against a node the proof
producer does not control, and wait out reorg depth.

